type: software
title: "The sharp upper edge of the normalised distance Laplacian"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. For the normalised distance Laplacian of a connected graph (Reinhart), the maximum of the largest eigenvalue over graphs of order n is 2 - 4/sqrt(3n) + o(n^-1/2), answering the order-of-magnitude question of Johnston and Tait. Every sequence attaining this rate looks, at the scale of its diameter, like a path of length (sqrt3 + o(1)) sqrt(n) with half of the vertices in nearly complete subgraphs at each end. Sharp constants follow for every fixed power of the distance, for trees (4 sqrt(2/3) at power one) and for graphs excluding a fixed subgraph with a cycle. Exhaustive computation: among all trees with 6 to 20 vertices the maximiser is two stars joined by a path. First order only; Reinhart's exact conjecture stays open."
